  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Hours now carry the noun ('یوه بجه', 'دوه بجې', ...) so 1 o'clock gets the correct feminine singular 'یوه بجه' instead of 'یو بجې'. All minutes are additive: 'درې بجې او لس دقیقې'. Compromises: :30 is 'درې بجې او دېرش دقیقې' rather than the idiomatic 'درې نیمې بجې' (نیمې must sit between hour and بجې, impossible with the noun inside {h}); no subtractive 'to' phrases because they require the oblique hour ('څلورو بجو ته'), which the schema cannot produce. Doubts: whether 'دقیقې' or the colloquial 'منټه' is preferred; overall Pashto phrasing is best effort."
    }
  ]
